<title>RUSSIA: Russian non-CIS crude oil exports rise in June.</title>
<headline>Russian non-CIS crude oil exports rise in June.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian exports of crude oil to countries outside the Commonwealth of Independent States rose to 9.67 million tonnes (roughly 2.32 million barrels per day) in June from 8.92 million tonnes (some 2.14 million bpd) in May, State Statistics Committee figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>EXPORTS TO NON-CIS DESTINATIONS (THOUSANDS OF TONNES)</p>
<p>			     June 1996   May 1996   June 1995</p>
<p>    Crude oil		 9,672	8,924	 n/a</p>
<p>    Gasoline		    283	  288	 n/a</p>
<p>    Diesel fuel	     1,555	1,861	 n/a</p>
<p>    Fuel oil (mazut)	1,373	1,800	 n/a</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
